CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ functional cast to dependent tuple_element type: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
Fixed 2026-07-28: (a) a typename-qualified name is never a
constructor declarator-id ([temp.res.general]/4), so the functional
cast statement no longer parses as a constructor declaration; (b) the
mem-initializer parameter-collision path derives the class scope from
`this` ([class.base.init]/2) instead of blindly indexing id_map with
an instantiated member template's empty/foreign class_identifier
(null-scope dereference).
